  }, {
    "circumstance" : {
      "context" : "Statement 5 under review (from 2026-09-15 cutover review)"
    },
    "exact" : "I quoted the Dockside number — the exception queue not flattening until day nine or ten. I went back through the Dockside logs on Friday because Xavier's comment about it being one site, one season was bothering me. The reason the queue took nine days to flatten at Dockside is that the old reconciliation job ran weekly and every run threw a fresh batch of exceptions. Two weeks was two reconciliation cycles. It was never about the site settling.",
    "local_id" : "src-10",
    "act" : "assertive",
    "prefix" : "ll me why.\n  > **Tina Team:** ",
    "footing_case" : null,
    "suffix" : "\n\n#### 5. <https://aswritten.a",
    "note" : null,
    "redacted" : false,
    "actor" : "Tina TeamMember"
  }, {
    "circumstance" : {
      "context" : "Statement 6 under review (from 2026-09-15 cutover review)"
    },
    "exact" : "That job is gone. It was retired in July. Nothing in the new platform runs on a weekly cycle — reconciliation is continuous now. So the number I gave was measuring a job that doesn't exist any more, and I attached it to the soak as though it were a property of the site.",
    "local_id" : "src-11",
    "act" : "assertive",
    "prefix" : "b is gone.\n  > **Tina Team:** ",
    "footing_case" : null,
    "suffix" : "\n\n#### 6. <https://aswritten.a",
    "note" : null,
    "redacted" : false,
    "actor" : "Tina TeamMember"
  }, {
    "circumstance" : {
      "context" : "Statement 7 under review (from 2026-09-15 cutover review)"
    },
    "exact" : "One week. Strip the reconciliation cycles out of the Dockside curve and the underlying exception rate is flat by day four. One week gives you the flattening plus three days to look at it, which is the same margin I was arguing for. One week is the soak, and please don't hold the plan to two weeks on my say-so, because I was wrong on the eighth.",
    "local_id" : "src-12",
    "act" : "assertive",
    "prefix" : " the soak?\n  > **Tina Team:** ",
    "footing_case" : null,
    "suffix" : "\n\n#### 7. <https://aswritten.a",
    "note" : null,
    "redacted" : false,
    "actor" : "Tina TeamMember"
  }, {
    "circumstance" : {
      "context" : "Statement 8 under review (from 2026-09-15 cutover review)"
    },
    "exact" : "Can I say that I think this is the right correction and also that it costs us something? Two weeks was conservative in a place where being conservative was cheap. One week is defensible but it has no slack in it.",
    "local_id" : "src-13",
    "act" : "assertive",
    "prefix" : "s had.\n\n  The statement:\n\n  > ",
    "footing_case" : null,
    "suffix" : "\n\n  The lines after it:\n\n  > *",
